      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You are absolutely right to point out this significant humanitarian cost, as it remains one of the primary ethical critiques of modern sanctions. Many scholars now favor \"precision sanctions,\" which target elite networks rather than the general population, to minimize harm to civilians. Ultimately, the debate often hinges on whether the moral imperative of regime change outweighs the tragedy of civilian suffering, a complex dilemma there is no single solution for.",
      "source": "target",
